                    <encodingDesc>
                              <projectDesc>
                                        <p>This manuscript text has been encoded according to the standard set out in <title>The Menota handbook</title> (version 3.0 beta), at <ref target="http://www.menota.org/HB3_index.xml"> http://www.menota.org/HB3_index.xml</ref> as of <date>2018-09-12</date>.</p>
                                        <p>The text has numbered pagebreaks and linebreaks according to Ludvig Holm-Olsen’s edition (referred to as ed="H-O"), Finnur Jónsson’s edition (referred to as
                                                  ed="FJ_utg") and numbered pagebreaks, columnbreaks and linebreaks according to the manuscript. The latter refers to the foliation of the manuscript,
                                                  e.g. 1r, 1v, 2r, 2v, etc. The later pagination of the mansucript has been given as values to the ed="AM" attribute, i.e. 1, 2, 3, 4, etc.</p>
                              </projectDesc>
                              <editorialDecl>
                                        <correction status="high">
                                                  <p>This text is based on the text in the slip collection of Gammelnorsk Ordboksverk and the text in Ludvig Holm Olsen’s edition and corrected against
                                                            the manuscript.</p>
                                        </correction>
                                        <normalization me:level="dipl">
                                                  <p>This text has been encoded on a diplomatic level.</p>
                                        </normalization>
                                        <interpretation me:lemmatized="completely" me:morphAnalyzed="completely">
                                                  <p>Approx. two thirds of the text has been lemmatised and morphologically analysed by the Gammelnorsk Ordboksverk at the University of Oslo and then
                                                            transformed according to the rules specified in ch. 11 of the Menota Handbook, v. 3.0. The remaining one third of the text was partly lemmatised and
                                                            morphologically analysed by <persName>Juliane Marie-Thérèse Tiemann</persName>, and later supplied and corrected by <persName>Eiríkur Kristjánsson</persName>,
                                                            <persName>Þorsteinn Vilhjálmsson</persName> and <persName>Fartein Th. Øverland</persName>. The whole text, apart from the Latin section, 
                                                            has now been annotated for morphology. In a parallel project, Menotec, the whole text has been annotated for syntax by <persName>Eiríkur Kristjánsson</persName>,
                                                            <persName>Þorsteinn Vilhjálmsson</persName> and <persName>Fartein Th. Øverland</persName> in the period 2019-2021.</p>
                                        </interpretation>
                              </editorialDecl>
