                              <div type="major-section"><head><supplied>Prologue</supplied></head>
                                        <div type="part">
                                                  
                                                  
                                                  <p>
                                                            <gap extent="2" unit="leaf"></gap><pb ed="AM" n="1"/>
                                                            <pb ed="ms" n="1r"/>
                                                            <cb ed="ms" n="a"/>
                                                            <gap extent="16" unit="line"></gap>
                                                            <lb n="1" ed="FJ_utg"/>
                                                  </p>
                                        </div>

                                        <note type="explanatory">The three first leaves of the first quire of AM 243 bα fol have been lost, apart from a small strip of the third leaf. The prologue of
                                                  Konungs skuggsjá may have been part of this lacuna, and in Ludvig Holm-Olsen’s edition (1945), the prologue is transcribed after the later Icelandic
                                                  manuscript AM 243 e fol and is rendered on pp. 1.01–2.41.</note>

                                        
                              </div>
                              <div type="major-section"><head><supplied>First part: The merchant and the natural world</supplied></head>
                                        <div type="part"><head><supplied>1. The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom</supplied></head>
                                                  
                                                  <p>
